menu "c6_car project"

    config C6_FACTORY_DEV_OVERRIDE
        bool "BENCH ONLY: synthesize factory data when NVS is empty"
        default y
        help
            Lets a bench board come up as SD-DEV000 with a fixed password when
            no production provisioning was written.  MUST be disabled (n) for
            production builds (LLDD 4.1 FACTORY_WAIT semantics).

    config C6_MAINT_BLE
        bool "Enable BLE DPT maintenance channel (NimBLE)"
        default n
        help
            LLDD 4.9: NimBLE GATT service for the production fixture.
            Requires CONFIG_BT_ENABLED=y (build with sdkconfig.maint or set
            it manually).  Consumer builds keep this off (open question Q3).

    config C6_BENCH_BOD_DISABLE
        bool "BENCH ONLY: disable brownout detector (weak bench supply)"
        default n
        help
            Brownout fires at Wi-Fi power-up (~400 ms, RF calibration current
            peak) when the bench supply sags below 2.51 V - the LOWEST
            threshold level available on ESP32-C6 (SEL_7), so there is no
            softer step.  This option calls esp_brownout_disable() at the
            earliest point of app_main.  Risk: flash writes and RF calibration
            run outside the guaranteed voltage window - bench bring-up only,
            NEVER for production builds, and fix the supply first if possible.

    config C6_BENCH_CTRL
        bool "BENCH ONLY: control bypass (no pairing, DRIVE->SET_SPEED, C6 heartbeat)"
        default n
        help
            Bench bring-up shortcut while the TC275 build still refuses 0x50
            DRIVE and the PAIR channel (myCar link_dispatch whitelist).  With
            this on:  every WS session is promoted to CTRL without a token;
            v2 DRIVE (0x50 v,omega) is translated on the C6 into SET_SPEED
            (0x10 left,right percent), the one op CPU0 already executes; and
            the bridge injects a 0x21 HEARTBEAT every 60 ms so CPU0's 100 ms
            heartbeat watchdog stays fed.  MUST be disabled (n) for production
            builds - it removes the pairing gate and changes the wire op.

    config C6_NET_START_DELAY_MS
        int "Delay before Wi-Fi start (voltage settling, ms)"
        default 0
        range 0 5000
        help
            Bench mitigation: let the supply recover from the boot surge
            before the RF power-up peak.  0 = no delay (production default).

    config C6_WIFI_TX_POWER_QDBM
        int "Max Wi-Fi TX power, 0.25 dBm units (0 = chip default)"
        default 0
        range 0 84
        help
            Bench mitigation for weak supplies: caps the transmit power and
            with it the PA current peak (e.g. 40 = 10 dBm).  0 keeps the
            chip default (~20 dBm) - production stays 0.

    config C6_LEGACY_TCP
        bool "Enable TCP 8080 legacy raw-frame bridge"
        default n
        help
            LLDD FR-10: proto v2 frames over TCP 8080 for demo clients.
            Recommended only for the first production batches (Q4).

endmenu
